		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=3022&amp;p=35149#p35149"><![CDATA[
Hey,<br>After reading this thread I ordered a GPS module from Aliexpress (<a href="https://vi.aliexpress.com/item/1005001704030454.html" class="postlink">https://vi.aliexpress.com/item/1005001704030454.html</a>), which is I think small enough to fit in the radio.<br>It hasn't arrived yet, but I would like to ask you about the connections.<br>Someone mentioned that it would need a transistor to power the GPS module, as the pins can't provide enough current. However, I checked the datasheet of the MCU and it states the "absolute maximum current rating" of that pin is 25mA, which should be enough for the module (on the product page, it shows &lt;25mA @3.3V).<br>Any suggestions or comments on this? Is it possible that I wouldn't need a transistor, or just do it to be safe?<br>Thanks in advance.<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=6043">HA7VM</a> — Wed Jan 15, 2025 2:23 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
